<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">morbĭdus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		morbus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Sickly, diseased</i> (rare and only ante-class. and
			post-Aug.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">syn. aeger, aegrotus): apes morbidae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 16, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 26, 40, § 96</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Sickly, unwholesome</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 1225</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aër,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					6, 1097</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					6, 1261</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
